  offerDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - Now that you understand load transfer, let's put that knowledge to use.
    - This crossing is different from the ones you've handled before.
    - The gap is <b><#E09500>100 meters</color></b> wide.
    - A jeep will use this route during the test.
    - The site already has wooden towers, and you now have rope available for your
      design.
    - <b><#E09500>The towers, rope, and anchor points give you another way to support
      parts of the bridge across the canyon</color></b>.
    - You don't have to build the same way you did on your earlier projects.
    - Remember what we discussed about load transfer.
    - <b><#E09500>Pay attention to how the vehicle's weight travels through the connected
      parts of your bridge and toward its supports</color></b>.
    - Think carefully about how you connect the different components.
    - If you're ready, take the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - You've got the towers, anchor points, and rope available at the site.
    - <b><#E09500>Think about how you can use them to support the structure across
      the gap</color></b>.
    - Remember, the load needs a continuous path through the structure and toward
      its supports.
    - How you connect everything is up to you.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - That's it.
    - The eastern passage is open.
    - You started by connecting Central Canyonville to the factory.
    - Then you improved the route through the canyon and brought it all the way to
      the community.
    - This last crossing asked you to use the site differently from the ones before
      it.
    - You also got to see how the different parts of a bridge work together to carry
      and transfer weight.
    - <b><#E09500>Remember those towers and how they helped support a crossing over
      a wider gap</color></b>.
    - You may encounter structures like that again.
    - Now the route leads toward <b><#E09500>Town River</color></b>.
    - Head there when you're ready.
    - Good work, {PlayerName}.
    - If our paths cross again, I may still have something for you.
